<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Santarém, Portugal</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santarem">Santarém</a> is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tagus">Tagus</a> in central Portugal, north-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a>, above a fertile river plain. As Roman Scallabis it was an administrative centre, and under Muslim rule a frontier fortress that changed hands several times. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-i-of-kongo">Afonso I</a> took it for Portugal in a surprise attack in March 1147, shortly before Lisbon, and medieval kings often held their cortes there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/santarem-portugal.jpg" alt="Santarém, Portugal" width="320" height="172" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Concierge.2C · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Santar%C3%A9m_-_Igreja_do_Semin%C3%A1rio_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
